1
00:04:37,894 --> 00:04:43,894
It's Big Adventure! It's Big Laughs! It's Big Bird on the Big Screen!

2
00:09:15,789 --> 00:09:21,789
Follow That Bird is a family, comedy, adventure film directed by Ken Kwapis.

3
00:13:53,684 --> 00:13:59,684
Big Bird is sent to live far from Sesame Street by a pesky social worker, who
thinks it would be better for him to live with other birds.

4
00:18:31,578 --> 00:18:37,578
Unhappy, Big Bird runs away from his foster home, prompting the rest of the
Sesame Street gang to go on a cross-country journey to find him.

5
00:23:09,473 --> 00:23:15,473
Big Bird / Oscar the Grouch / Bruno the Trashman
(voice), played by Caroll Spinney.

6
00:27:47,368 --> 00:27:53,368
Kermit the Frog / Ernie (voice), played by Jim Henson.

7
00:32:25,263 --> 00:32:31,263
Cookie Monster / Bert / Grover / Additional Muppets (voice), played by Frank Oz.

8
00:37:03,157 --> 00:37:09,157
Gladys the Cow / Feathered Friends Owl / Additional Muppets
/ Grouches (voice), played by Richard Hunt.

9
00:41:41,052 --> 00:41:47,052
Feathered Friends Magistrate / Grouch Diner Patron / Little Girl /
Additional Muppets (voice), played by Kathryn Mullen.

10
00:46:18,947 --> 00:46:24,947
Count von Count / Herry Monster / Additional
Muppets (voice), played by Jerry Nelson.

11
00:50:56,842 --> 00:51:02,842
Sesame Street Presents: Follow That Bird (or simply Follow That Bird) is a 1985 American family
musical comedy film directed by Ken Kwapis, and written by Tony Geiss and Judy Freudberg.

12
00:55:34,736 --> 00:55:40,736
Based on the children's television series Sesame Street, it
was the series' first theatrical feature film.

13
01:00:12,631 --> 01:00:18,631
It stars Muppet performers Caroll Spinney, Jim Henson and Frank Oz alongside Sandra
Bernhard, John Candy, Chevy Chase, Joe Flaherty, Waylon Jennings, and Dave Thomas.

14
01:04:50,526 --> 01:04:56,526
It was filmed at the Cinespace Film Studios and on
location in the Greater Toronto Area.

15
01:09:28,421 --> 01:09:34,421
Follow That Bird was theatrically released in the United States on
August 2, 1985, by Warner Bros., and grossed $14 million.

16
01:14:06,315 --> 01:14:12,315
It received mostly positive reviews from critics.

17
01:18:44,210 --> 01:18:50,210
The film explores themes of farm, friendship, airplane, airport, waitress.

18
01:23:22,105 --> 01:23:28,105
The tone is lighthearted.
